From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] combase: WinRT restricted error information, process activation factories, COM security, suspended class objects

WinRT error reporting (documented in roerrorapi.h/restrictederrorinfo.h;
the functions were stubs or "@ stub" exports, so error information never
existed and some calls ended the program):
- RoOriginateError, RoOriginateErrorW and RoOriginateLanguageException
  make a restricted error object for a failure: its error, the system's
  description of it, the message given (at most 512 characters), a
  reference and the language exception, told to a debugger (exception
  0x40080201 when one is attached or exceptions are forced). It becomes
  the thread's error information, as an IErrorInfo too.
- GetRestrictedErrorInfo takes it from the thread (S_FALSE when there is
  none), SetRestrictedErrorInfo sets one, RoClearError clears it.
- RoTransformError(W) make the new error's object after the old one
  (ILanguageExceptionErrorInfo2::GetPreviousLanguageExceptionErrorInfo).
- RoGetMatchingRestrictedErrorInfo gives the thread's object for the
  error or a new one; RoResolveRestrictedErrorInfoReference finds a
  recent one by its reference; RoCaptureErrorContext marks it.
- RoSetErrorReportingFlags keeps the flags (suppressing exceptions or the
  thread's error information), RoGetErrorReportingFlags gives them.
- RoFailFastWithErrorContext ends the process with the error.

Activation:
- RoRegisterActivationFactories and RoRevokeActivationFactories keep a
  process's own activation factories, which RoGetActivationFactory and
  RoActivateInstance use before the registry's (they were "semi-stubs";
  the factory pointer is now cleared on failure, which Wine's roapi test
  no longer marks as todo).

COM:
- CoInitializeSecurity sets the process's security once; a second call
  returns RPC_E_TOO_LATE (it said yes to everything).
- Class objects registered with REGCLS_SUSPENDED reach the SCM, and
  other processes, only after CoResumeClassObjects; CoSuspendClassObjects
  takes them back (both were stubs that said yes).
- Proxies implement IForegroundTransfer, letting the object's server
  process take the foreground; CoAllowSetForegroundWindow uses it, and
  refuses objects that are not proxies with E_NOINTERFACE (a stub).

Gate: test/roerror-gate.sh (64- and 32-bit, test/roerror-probe.c).
Mutants SG_MUTANT_NO_RESTRICTED_ERROR, SG_MUTANT_NO_REGISTERED_FACTORIES
(combase/roapi.c), SG_MUTANT_SECURITY_ALWAYS_OK, SG_MUTANT_NO_RESUME
(combase/combase.c).
